{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 4, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 7769957715678686303, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 632, "mtime": 1791865359.0789583, "sha256": "dadccbb0e197439ff1d5cd8f4310073f2fd4ebf60604a282915551427b1db68b"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 361, "mtime": 1791865362.7391062, "sha256": "801fa500f340f66bbc20e1a6c21eb5400237bda651df6955702441539e0840e0"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-38/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/4/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-38/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/4/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running it.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`. On top of that, Python's `round()` rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, so the docstring's \"half up\" rule never applied. With the old code, `round(0.125, 2)` gave `0.12` and `round(1.005, 2)` gave `1.0`.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now turns the number into a `Decimal` using the decimal form Python prints for it (`\"2.675\"`), not its binary value. It then rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` and returns a float, so callers like `add_vat` don't change. Negative amounts round away from zero: `-2.675` gives `-2.68`.\n\n**Tests:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, which checks `2.675 \u2192 2.68`, `0.125 \u2192 0.13`, `1.005 \u2192 1.01` and `2.674 \u2192 2.67`. pytest isn't installed here, so I called the test functions directly with `python3`. The new test and the existing `test_split` both pass. I ran plain `round()` to confirm it gives the old wrong values; I didn't run the new test against the old code, because the directory has no git history to revert to.\n\n`split()` has a similar problem in `int(total * 100)`: it cuts off instead of rounding, so a total like `0.29` can lose a cent. I left it alone because it's outside this fix.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 197936, "requests_cache_write": 64684, "requests_cost_usd": 0.41136720000000004, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2414, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial4", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 7, "score":